#     `[button,a]:focus-visible:ring-ring/50`. An interactive bubble takes `base.css`'s one 2px
#     `:focus-visible` outline like every other control; upstream's `outline-none` would have
#     suppressed it outright, which is why the glow had to exist.
#   FOC-6: `bubbleReactionsVariants` swaps upstream's RESTING `ring-3 ring-card` for
#     `outline-3 outline-card`. FOC-6 is "never a box-shadow ring or glow anywhere" and it names
#     Bubble by name; a Tailwind `ring` IS a box-shadow. The outline paints the identical 3px
#     band in the identical token, outside the border box and following the radius, and the chip
#     is a non-focusable `<div>` so it can never collide with the focus outline.
#   A11Y-2: audited, NO HUNK. Nothing in this file is a pointer target of its own — `Bubble`,
#     `BubbleGroup` and `BubbleReactions` are `<div>`s, and `BubbleContent` becomes a control
#     only when the call site renders one into it, at which point the control's own size is the
#     call site's. `bubble.test.tsx` measures the interactive-bubble fixture against the floor.
#   cn: `import { cn } from "cn"` becomes `@vegastack/design` — our npm layer owns `cn` (DOC-2).
#   formatting: the repository formatter (prettier defaults: semicolons, trailing commas)
#               reflows the file, and `registry-stamp.mjs` writes the provenance header the
#               three-copy model needs (DOC-1); those hunks carry no decision of their own.
